  "query_preview": "..\nIssued at 201 AM CDT Thu Sep 3 2026\n\nSimilar conditions as yesterday are expected today across South \nTexas, with convection from TD Edouard remaining to our northeast \nand heat concerns growing this afternoon. Another Heat Advisory is \nin effect along the inland Coastal Bend and Victoria County where \nheat indices of 110 or greater are expected for at least 2 hours \nthis afternoon. In addition, elevated fire weather conditions will \nbe present over the Brush Country with relative humidity dropping \nbelow 30% mid-afternoon and evening.\n\nRemnants of Edouard aloft will shift southwesterly into South Texas \nlate tonight into Friday, meandering over the area through Labor Day \nWeekend, before moving well into Mexico as an inverted trough rides \nthe southern periphery of the ridge originating out of the SE CONUS \nearly next week. These two features: remnants of Edouard and \nadditional mid-level trough ushering 75th percentile moisture (PWATs \naround 2.0\"), will result in widespread daily low rain chances (20-\n35%) beginning Friday or Saturday, with greater chances (35-60%) \nover the Victoria Crossroads. Diurnal seabreeze convection tapping \ninto the mid-level lift support and enhanced moisture will allow for \npopcorn like showers and storms along outflows.\n\nThe additional sky cover and rain chances with the increased \nmoisture this weekend into next week will hopefully lower \ntemperatures a few degrees and therefore lower the overall heat risk.",
